\description{
Fits K latent clusters. Within cluster k the clustering features follow
\code{N(mu_k, Sigma_k)} and survival follows a Cox model with coefficients
\code{beta_k}. By default all clusters share one Breslow baseline hazard, so
clusters differ only in their survival \emph{mechanism} (\code{beta_k}) and in
their feature profile (\code{mu_k}, \code{Sigma_k}).
}
\details{
The EM algorithm alternates:
\itemize{
\item \strong{E-step.} \code{tau_ik} is proportional to
\verb{pi_k N(x_gmm_i | mu_k, Sigma_k) f_k(t_i, d_i | x_cox_i)^gamma}.
\item \strong{M-step.} Closed-form \code{pi}, \code{mu}, \code{Sigma}; the shared baseline by
weighted Breslow; then each \code{beta_k} by a tau-weighted ridge fit of the
Poisson working model with offset \verb{log Lambda0(t)}.
}

\strong{What gamma does.} \code{gamma} sets how much a subject's own outcome
counts when deciding which cluster they belong to. With \code{gamma = 0},
membership comes from the clustering features alone, so clusters that
differ only in mechanism (and not in feature profile) cannot be found.
With \code{gamma = 1} (the generative model, and the default) the outcome is
weighted as in the joint likelihood. \code{gamma} is fixed rather than tuned:
data-driven selectors either chose \code{gamma = 0} or inflated false
discovery in simulation.

\strong{Baseline and centring.} Cox features are centred at their training
means before fitting, so the baseline hazard is the hazard of a subject
whose \code{X_cox} equals the training means, and cluster k's hazard is
\verb{lambda0(t) exp((x - xbar)' beta_k)}. With a shared baseline this matters:
because \verb{xbar' beta_k} differs between clusters, the centred and uncentred
mixture predictors differ by a subject-specific amount, and only the
centred one pairs with the fitted baseline. The means are stored in
\code{cox_scaler$center}. The overall level of the linear predictor is not
identified separately from the baseline, so compare linear predictors
only up to a constant.

\strong{What is estimable.} When clusters differ only in mechanism, individual
labels are not consistently recoverable, but the coefficient contrast
\code{beta_1 - beta_2} is. Test K = 2 against K = 1 with
\code{\link[=gemcox_heterogeneity_test]{gemcox_heterogeneity_test()}}, not by cross-validated C-index.
}
